note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Pure seeded OM-2 Visor lane 4: structured six-row verification report, a port of
note src/visor/visor_verify.c together with the verification it calls: omega_validate.c
note (object and graph validation), omega_verify.c (V0 structural, V1 differential, V2
note properties), omega_realize.c / omega_realize_synth.c (realization ids) and the
note program contract check of omega_program.c.
note Depends on visor.om, visor_machine.om, om/aarch64/aarch64_om2.om (a64validate,
note a64decode), om/visor/verify_om2.om (om_ver_*) and om/visor/validate_om2.om (om_val_*).
note
note C arguments become explicit state, as the C pointers they replace:
note   SemanticId *id            -> vver_qid (32 bytes); the graph is the v_og store
note   RealizationObject *real   -> a realization slot 0..7 (vver_r*), or -1 for NULL
note   OmegaMachineGraph *mg     -> a visor_machine graph slot (vmch_g*), or -1 for NULL
note   OmegaProgram *p           -> the program record vver_p_* (has_p 0 for NULL)
note V1 runs the realization on an interpreter of the decoded AArch64 subset the
note realizers emit (ADD SUB MUL AND ORR EOR register forms with their shifts, MOVZ,
note MOVK, RET); OM-2 has no host word to map and call native code, which is what
note omega_exec_native_f3 does. An instruction outside that subset returns rc=-3.

const VVER_RN ulong 8
const VVER_CB ulong 4096
const VVER_ROWS ulong 6

